From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] difxapi: DriverPackagePreinstall, Install, Uninstall, GetPath and the log callbacks

All twelve entry points were stubs; Preinstall, Install and Uninstall returned
ERROR_SUCCESS having done nothing. Now, as Microsoft's DIFxAPI pages describe:

Every function first refuses a 32-bit caller (ERROR_IN_WOW64), bad arguments
(ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER: a NULL path, unknown flags, an INSTALLERINFO with an
empty string), a path past the maximum (ERROR_FILENAME_EXCED_RANGE) or that is
not fully qualified (ERROR_INVALID_NAME), a caller who is not an administrator
(ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED), a missing INF (ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND), and an INF in the
system INF directory (ERROR_CANT_ACCESS_FILE).

DriverPackagePreinstall / Install put the package in the driver store -- an
unsigned package (no catalog named) is TRUST_E_NOSIGNATURE, a catalog named
and missing CRYPT_E_FILE_ERROR, a package without a [Manufacturer] section
ERROR_INVALID_FUNCTION, a package that is already there ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS
unless DRIVER_PACKAGE_REPAIR -- and Install then installs it (through newdev)
on the devices present that it is a better match for, or on every device it
matches with DRIVER_PACKAGE_FORCE: ERROR_NO_SUCH_DEVINST when no device
matches (the package stays preinstalled), ERROR_NO_MORE_ITEMS when the devices
have better drivers. With DRIVER_PACKAGE_ONLY_IF_DEVICE_PRESENT the package is
kept only if it matches a device. An INSTALLERINFO associates an application
with the package (kept in HKLM\Software\Wine\DIFx).

DriverPackageUninstall removes the caller's association; while other applications
need the package it stays (ERROR_DEPENDENT_APPLICATIONS_EXIST) unless
DRIVER_PACKAGE_FORCE; a package not in the store is
ERROR_DRIVER_PACKAGE_NOT_IN_STORE. DriverPackageGetPath returns the INF in the
driver store, with ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER and the size for a buffer too
small.

DIFXAPISetLogCallback and SetDifxLogCallback register the one callback that
is called with the events of an operation (information, success, error with
the Win32 error); NULL unregisters.

difxapi now imports setupapi and advapi32.
---
--- a/dlls/difxapi/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/difxapi/Makefile.in
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 MODULE = difxapi.dll
+IMPORTS = setupapi advapi32
 
